[[:db/cas 17592186100700 :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM =\n\t{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & - 3\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-3)-3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $\\det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA = |{-9}| = 9\n$$" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM =\n\t{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & - 3\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-3)-3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $\\det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA = |{-9}| = 9\n$$"]]
